<title>CHILE: Chilean copper exports rise sharply in June.</title>
<headline>Chilean copper exports rise sharply in June.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper exports rose to $649 million in June from $538 million in the same month last year as the result of a rally in world copper prices, said the Central Bank in its monthly report.</p>
<p>&quot;Copper prices were higher in June than in the same month last year for the first time since November 1995,&quot; said the report.  </p>
<p>The bank figures showed copper exports rising 18 percent in the first six months of the year, reflecting a sharp increase in production as prices were lower in the first half of the year than in the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>The following are details of Chile's mining exports in June.</p>
<p>METAL			  June 1997	   June 1996</p>
<p> Copper			  648.9		 537.5</p>
<p> Iron			     10.0		  19.7</p>
<p> Salitre and iodine	   21.6		   7.2</p>
<p> Silver			   13.0		  12.0</p>
<p> Molybdenum		     26.8		  18.9</p>
<p> Lithium carbonate	     4.3		   3.9</p>
<p> Metallic gold and dore     33.9		  33.1</p>
<p> Gold mineral		    6.2		  -1.2</p>
<p> Others			    8.3		   5.9</p>
<p> TOTAL			   773.0		 637.0</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
